pod_rpg.guide.changelog.3.0.0=- Added Classes%1  - 10 new Classes that specialize in different Skills %1  - Check out the Guide Book for more information%1- Skills in the Guide Book will now be sorted based on their class%1- Reworked Item Binding System%1  - Players can now define their own Bindings and modify/delete existing Bindings%1  - Added the option for bindings to enable specific abilities%1  - Added the option for bindings to show the levelling progress of a skill%1  - Check out the 'Bindings' Menu in the Guide Book for more information!%1- Divided 'Settings' into 'Player Settings' and 'Global Settings'%1  - Player Settings are individual to each player%1  - Global Settings will affect all Players and can only be modified by permitted Players%1- Added player setting that allows to adjust the maximum input time between key inputs%1- Added player setting that allows to change the display slot of the current input sequence%1- Added player setting that allows to change the display slot of the partly matched bindings%1- Added dynamic default values for Player Settings: Certain Player Settings will by default load with values adjusted to the player's device%1- Added 'Skill Options' for every Skill%1  - Skill Options are individual for every player%1  - Added an option to disable a skill%1  - Added an option to disable the passive ability of a skill%1  - Added an option to hide the progress bar of a skill when gaining exp%1  - Removed 'Double Jump' from the Player Settings (this can now be done through the skill options)%1  - Removed 'Explorer Exp Bar' from the Player Settings (this can now be done through the skill options)%1- Pale Oak Wood Blocks will now work in any wood related Skills and Abilities.%1- Players will now only receive EXP from the Pyromaniac Skill when the Flint and Steel actually loses durability.%1- Netherite Armor now no longer affects Double Jump.%1- Netherite Armor now no longer affects the TNT Boost Ability.%1- Added prevention that removes the fog from the Homecoming Ability whenever a player rejoins a world.%1- Fixed Homecoming Ability teleporting the player to a really high location when teleporting to the world spawn.%1- Fixed certain loot being unavailable in the Sunken Treasure Ability.%1- Fixed a bug related to enchantments on items from the Sunken Treasure Ability loot.%1- Fixed Super Fertilizer not growing certain Crops.%1
pod_rpg.class.unskilled.name=Unskilled
pod_rpg.class.unskilled.description=If you're not ready to choose a class and you want to just level up your skills undisturbed then unskilled is for you! There are no buffs or debuffs.
pod_rpg.class.mage.name=Mage
pod_rpg.class.mage.description=Magic hangs in the air around you, focus on skills with a magical touch.
pod_rpg.class.ranger.name=Ranger
pod_rpg.class.ranger.description=As a ranger you'll silently creep through forests and have a sneaking advantage!
pod_rpg.class.demolitionist.name=Demolitionist
pod_rpg.class.demolitionist.description=If you love the smell of gunpowder, and if tnt is your best weapon, then you're a Demolitionist.
pod_rpg.class.dwarf.name=Dwarf
pod_rpg.class.dwarf.description=Caves are your best friend, if you'd rather spend your days surrounded by rock then you're definitely a dwarf!
pod_rpg.class.warden.name=Warden
pod_rpg.class.warden.description=The guardian of the forest, you hear the weeping woods and long to live surrounded by trees.
pod_rpg.class.tidecaller.name=Tidecaller
pod_rpg.class.tidecaller.description=The waves crash through you, and you prefer swimming over walking.
pod_rpg.class.brute.name=Brute
pod_rpg.class.brute.description=When battle commences you're the first to charge, and the last to leave.
pod_rpg.class.harvestborn.name=Harvestborn
pod_rpg.class.harvestborn.description=Born to grow food, you prefer tending your crops and seeing life grow all around.
pod_rpg.class.wayfinder.name=Wayfinder
pod_rpg.class.wayfinder.description=Wayfinders are the explorers, the adventurers, who want to wake up in a new place every day.
pod_rpg.class.update_prompt=Introducing Classes! You've spent a lifetime exploring your world and building your skills, classes bring a new way to experience RPG Skills, by picking a class you can specialize in skills to give extra boosts but be warned every class have certain skills they're also no longer able to use.
